{
  "title": "Build - Local Invoice Review POC in GitHub Copilot",
  "locked": true,
  "description": "Local proof of concept chapter in GitHub Copilot that shows the first invoice-review agent taking shape, running with local or simulated data, comparing local and cloud execution, and demonstrating sandbox protection before the Foundry handoff.",
  "rows": [
    {
      "locked": true,
      "locks": {
        "time": true,
        "narrative": true,
        "demo_actions": true,
        "screenshot": true,
        "visual": true,
        "design_plan": true
      },
      "time": "~35s",
      "narrative": "- Let's take a look at the GitHub Copilot app.\n- This is where I can work with Copilot without juggling multiple CLI sessions or SDKs.\n- If I decide to go deeper, I can hand any of these sessions directly into VS Code and continue developing there.\n- Everything starts from the home screen.\n- I get a high level view of active work, open issues, pending reviews, and any automations I've configured.\n- It is essentially my Copilot command center, and it is where I start every morning.",
      "demo_actions": "Open the GitHub Copilot app. Briefly orient the viewer to the home screen and top-level navigation. Pause long enough to call out active work, issues, reviews, and automations.",
      "screenshot": ".cutready/screenshots/20260617_111553_CleanShot 2026-06-17 at 11.15.31@2x.png"
    },
    {
      "locked": true,
      "locks": {
        "time": true,
        "narrative": true,
        "demo_actions": true,
        "screenshot": true,
        "visual": true,
        "design_plan": true
      },
      "time": "~40s",
      "narrative": "- Let me show you how I kicked off a proof of concept for our internal project, Pharma Shield.\n- All I need to do is enter a prompt: \"Start the contract reconciliation proof of concept.\"\n- From there, the Copilot app takes care of the setup.\n- The first thing you see is that it creates a worktree.\n- That gives me an isolated workspace so I can experiment freely without affecting my main branch or anyone else's work.",
      "demo_actions": "Move into the working area and enter the prompt to start the proof of concept. Show the setup beginning and briefly point out that a new worktree is being created.",
      "screenshot": ".cutready/screenshots/20260617_111801_CleanShot 2026-06-17 at 11.17.40@2x.png"
    },
    {
      "locked": true,
      "locks": {
        "time": true,
        "narrative": true,
        "demo_actions": true,
        "screenshot": true,
        "visual": true,
        "design_plan": true
      },
      "time": "~35s",
      "narrative": "- Next, it loads a custom skill I created specifically for this contract reconciliation scenario.\n- That skill carries the domain knowledge and the workflow, so every session starts with the same context instead of me rebuilding it each time.\n- Before anything runs, the app performs a quick preflight check of the local language model using Ollama.",
      "demo_actions": "Show the skill loading and the preflight check. Call out the custom skill for the scenario and the Ollama validation step.",
      "screenshot": ".cutready/screenshots/20260617_112228_CleanShot 2026-06-17 at 11.18.47@2x.png"
    },
    {
      "locked": true,
      "locks": {
        "time": true,
        "narrative": true,
        "demo_actions": true,
        "screenshot": true,
        "visual": true,
        "design_plan": true
      },
      "time": "~40s",
      "narrative": "- Once everything is ready, here is the application.\n- On the left is the Copilot session that's driving the work.\n- On the right is the Canvas, which gives me an interactive view of the application I'm building and testing.\n- Right now I'm using my local model, although I can switch to a cloud model at any time.",
      "demo_actions": "Open the Canvas and orient the viewer to the layout. Point out the Copilot session on the left, the interactive Canvas on the right, and the current model selection.",
      "screenshot": ".cutready/screenshots/20260617_112324_CleanShot 2026-06-17 at 11.20.38@2x.png"
    },
    {
      "locked": true,
      "locks": {
        "time": true,
        "narrative": true,
        "demo_actions": true,
        "screenshot": true,
        "visual": true,
        "design_plan": true
      },
      "time": "~40s",
      "narrative": "- That local setup matters because there are plenty of situations where I do not want to rely on cloud connectivity.\n- Maybe I'm on an airplane, working from a coffee shop, or handling sensitive customer data.\n- Running locally gives me lower latency, lets me work offline, and helps ensure that my data stays on the device during development and testing.\n- As soon as I submit the prompt, notice the live network monitor.\n- Every request is staying on the local machine, and there is no outbound traffic.",
      "demo_actions": "Submit a simple invoice question while the local model is selected. Keep the network monitor visible and show that requests stay on the device with no outbound traffic.",
      "screenshot": ".cutready/screenshots/20260617_112332_CleanShot 2026-06-17 at 11.20.07@2x.png"
    },
    {
      "locked": true,
      "locks": {
        "time": true,
        "narrative": true,
        "demo_actions": true,
        "screenshot": true,
        "visual": true,
        "design_plan": true
      },
      "time": "~35s",
      "narrative": "- From there, I can keep working through the proof of concept.\n- I can review flagged invoices, inspect the evidence trail behind each recommendation, approve recoveries, place items on hold, or escalate them for governance review.\n- This is the first proof that the invoice review flow is workable in a local proof of concept.",
      "demo_actions": "Walk through the invoice result in the Canvas. Show the recommendation, supporting evidence, and the available actions such as approve, hold, or escalate.",
      "screenshot": ".cutready/screenshots/20260617_112345_CleanShot 2026-06-17 at 11.21.34@2x.png"
    },
    {
      "locked": true,
      "locks": {
        "time": true,
        "narrative": true,
        "demo_actions": true,
        "screenshot": true,
        "visual": true,
        "design_plan": true
      },
      "time": "~30s",
      "narrative": "- Now let's compare that to using a cloud model.\n- I'll switch models, reload the Canvas, and run the exact same prompt.",
      "demo_actions": "Switch from the local model to a cloud model. Reload the Canvas and prepare to rerun the same invoice question.",
      "screenshot": null
    },
    {
      "locked": true,
      "locks": {
        "time": true,
        "narrative": true,
        "demo_actions": true,
        "screenshot": true,
        "visual": true,
        "design_plan": true
      },
      "time": "~35s",
      "narrative": "- This time, the network monitor tells a very different story.\n- We can see traffic leaving the device, along with which model was used, how many documents were sent, and how much data crossed the boundary.\n- That visibility makes it much easier to understand and audit what information is leaving the local environment.",
      "demo_actions": "Run the same prompt with the cloud model selected. Keep the network monitor visible and point out outbound requests, model details, document count, and data crossing the boundary.",
      "screenshot": null
    },
    {
      "locked": true,
      "locks": {
        "time": true,
        "narrative": true,
        "demo_actions": true,
        "screenshot": true,
        "visual": true,
        "design_plan": true
      },
      "time": "~30s",
      "narrative": "- One final capability I want to highlight is sandboxing.\n- Everything in this proof of concept is running inside an isolated execution environment called Microsoft MXC.",
      "demo_actions": "Return focus to the application security controls and point out the Microsoft MXC sandbox indicator. Set up the transition into the attack simulation.",
      "screenshot": null
    },
    {
      "locked": true,
      "locks": {
        "time": true,
        "narrative": true,
        "demo_actions": true,
        "screenshot": true,
        "visual": true,
        "design_plan": true
      },
      "time": "~35s",
      "narrative": "- To show why that matters, let's simulate a poisoned invoice containing a prompt injection attack that tries to access proprietary data, like a master batch record.\n- With the MXC sandbox enabled, the attack is blocked.\n- The Canvas explains exactly what happened.\n- Outbound network access is denied, file access is restricted, and the malicious prompt never reaches sensitive data.",
      "demo_actions": "Run the poisoned invoice scenario with the sandbox enabled. Show the blocked result and the Canvas explanation of denied network and file access.",
      "screenshot": null
    },
    {
      "locked": true,
      "locks": {
        "time": true,
        "narrative": true,
        "demo_actions": true,
        "screenshot": true,
        "visual": true,
        "design_plan": true
      },
      "time": "~35s",
      "narrative": "- Now let's disable the sandbox and run the same attack again.\n- This time, the trade secret is successfully exfiltrated.\n- The Canvas immediately identifies what happened, explains the impact, and the Copilot app automatically creates a GitHub issue documenting the incident.",
      "demo_actions": "Disable the sandbox and rerun the same attack. Show the exfiltration result, the explanation of impact, and the automatic GitHub issue creation.",
      "screenshot": null
    },
    {
      "locked": true,
      "locks": {
        "time": true,
        "narrative": true,
        "demo_actions": true,
        "screenshot": true,
        "visual": true,
        "design_plan": true
      },
      "time": "~20s",
      "narrative": "- I can open that issue immediately, assign it to the right engineer, or begin remediation myself.\n- Instead of just detecting the problem, the workflow moves directly into action.",
      "demo_actions": "Open the generated GitHub issue and briefly show assignment or remediation options.",
      "screenshot": null
    },
    {
      "locked": true,
      "locks": {
        "time": true,
        "narrative": true,
        "demo_actions": true,
        "screenshot": true,
        "visual": true,
        "design_plan": true
      },
      "time": "~20s",
      "narrative": "- At this point, we've proven that the idea works.\n- The next step is scaling it beyond a local proof of concept so the rest of the team can use it.\n- That's where cloud infrastructure comes in.\n- In the next demo, we'll take this same application and move it into Microsoft Foundry.",
      "demo_actions": "Pause on the completed flow and summarize what the local proof of concept established. Transition verbally to the next demo in Foundry.",
      "screenshot": null
    }
  ],
